      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Oh for sure, when you're the avatar creator you can control those things. My main concern is when using an avatar uploaded by someone else, and not knowing if the creator of said avatar kept that in mind when creating the Android version of the avatar.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-08-07T03:59:17.082Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Whenever I'm in a world with primarily Android users, I prefer to be in an Android compatible avatar. However, because I am on PCVR, I cannot tell if the PC version of the avatar has translated well into Android. Because of this, there have been many situations or accidents caused by not being able to see the Android version, some examples being: I'm not aware of an outfit I am wearing having not been added to the Android model, causing unwanted nudity, the Android version being an awkward version of the PC version, and many more.\n\nIt would also be helpful for avatar creators like myself to view the Android version of an avatar on PCVR. This is because the creator of the avatar may want to see the Android version of the avatar's performance in VRChat, and it is nearly impossible to do so with accurate results unless the creator uses an Android product themselves. \n\nThis feature would be extremely helpful for many PCVR players, whether they are casual VRChat players, or avatar creators. Thank you!",
